    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1506">

                <pb facs="1190" n="1180" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg1180"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.42700(R)/6–2449: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Cabot</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-06-24T19:00:00+08:00">June 24, 1949—7 p.
                            m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received June 25—2:39 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2475. <hi rendition="#italic">Shanghai Evening Post</hi> editor Gould announced
                    liquidation of paper yesterday press conference. Suspension publication June 15
                    initially due to wage dispute, later issue editorial freedom, after workers
                    refused to print news story giving Gould, version <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Post</hi> dispute (remytel 2313, June 17). Gould considered continued
                    newspaper operation futile when labor coercion attempted dictate contents of
                    paper. <pb facs="1191" n="1181" xml:id="pg1181"/> Gould and owner Starr<anchor
                        n="68" xml:id="d1506-f1"/> offered workers space in paper to give their
                    version of dispute. Gould’s final decision to liquidate based on recent attitude
                    of SMCC authorities regarding foreign papers as shown in <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >North China Daily News</hi> case reference story of mining Yangtze (remytel
                    2387, June 21<anchor n="69" xml:id="d1506-f2"/>) in which <hi
                        rendition="#italic">NCDN</hi> editor held personally responsible.</p>
                <p>VOA for background only.</p>
                <p>Sent Department; repeated Nanking 1345, OffEmb Canton 798.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cabot</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1506-f1" n="68" xml:id="d1506-f1-content">
                <p>Cornelius V. Starr, American citizen.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1506-f2" n="69" xml:id="d1506-f2-content">
